hadiths[16]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1067","that he found `Umar bin Al-Khattab in a group of people and he was swearing by his father. So Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) called them, saying, Verily! Allah forbids you to swear by your fathers. If one has to take an oath"
"1068","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, Whomever takes an oath in which he mentions Lat and `Uzza (forgetfully)"
"1069","My Companions sent me to Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) to ask him for some animals to ride on as they were accompanying him in the army of Al-Usra, and that was the Ghazwa (Battle) of Tabuk, I said, O Allah's Prophet! My companions have sent me to you to provide them with means of transportation."" He said"
"1070","I went to the Prophet (ﷺ) along with a group of Al-Ash`ariyin in order to request him to provide us with mounts. He said, By Allah"
"1071","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, O `Abdur-Rahman bin Samura! Do not seek to be a ruler"
"1072","(The Prophet) Solomon son of (the Prophet) David said, Tonight I will go round (i.e. have sexual relations with) one hundred women (my wives) everyone of whom will deliver a male child who will fight in Allah's Cause."" On that an Angel said to him"
"1073","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""Solomon (the son of) David said, 'Tonight I will sleep with seventy ladies each of whom will conceive a child who will be a knight fighting for ""Allah's Cause.' His companion said, 'If Allah will.' But Solomon did not say so; therefore none of those women got pregnant except one who gave birth to a half child."" The Prophet (ﷺ) further said, ""If the Prophet (ﷺ) Solomon had said it (i.e. 'If Allah will') he would have begotten children who would have fought in Allah's Cause."" Shuaib and Ibn Abi Az-Zinad said, ""Ninety (women) is more correct (than seventy)."
"1074","In the year of the Conquest of Mecca, the tribe of Khuza`a killed a man from the tribe of Bam Laith in revenge for a killed person belonging to them in the Pre-lslamic Period of Ignorance. So Allah's Apostle got up saying, Allah held back the (army having) elephants from Mecca"
"1075","I heard Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) saying, ""The reward of deeds depends upon the intentions and every person will get the reward according to what he has intended. So whoever emigrated for worldly benefits or for a woman to marry, his emigration was for what he emigrated for."""""
"1076","Narrated Abu Huraira:\n\nI heard Abu-l-Qasim (the Prophet) saying, \If somebody slanders his slave and the slave is free from \nwhat he says"
"1077","I saw Abu Dhar Al-Ghifari wearing a cloak, and his slave, too, was wearing a cloak. We asked him about that (i.e. how both were wearing similar cloaks). He replied, Once I abused a man and he complained of me to the Prophet (ﷺ) . The Prophet (ﷺ) asked me"
"1078","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""When your servant brings your food to you, if you do not ask him to join you, then at least ask him to take one or two handfuls, for he has suffered from its heat (while cooking it) and has taken pains to cook it nicely."""" ""1079"",Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said. While I was sleeping"
"1080","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, A pious slave gets a double reward."" Abu Huraira added: By Him in Whose Hands my soul is but for Jihad (i.e. holy battles)"
"1081","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, Goodness and comfort are for him who worships his Lord in a perfect manner and serves his master sincerely."""""""
"1082","`Umar asked the people, Who remembers the narration of the Prophet (ﷺ) about the affliction?"" Hudhaifa said ""1083"",Anas reported Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) as saying:If the son of Adam were to possess two valleys of riches. he would long for the third one. And the stomach of the son of Adam is not filled but with dust. And Allah returns to him who repents"
"1084","Jabir said: An Ansari man made his slave a Mudabbar and he had no other property than him. When the Prophet (ﷺ) heard of that, he said (to his companions), ""Who wants to buy him (i.e., the slave) for me?"" Nu'aim bin An-Nahham bought him for eight hundred Dirhams. I heard Jabir saying, ""That was a coptic slave who died in the same year."""""
